# 81. GOLDEN RULES TO REMEMBER

==================================================

1. range() excludes the stop value.

2. for loop is commonly used with iterables.

3. while loop depends on a condition.

4. Always update the control variable in a while loop.

5. break terminates the loop.

6. continue skips the current iteration.

7. pass does nothing.

8. Nested loops mean loop inside loop.

9. % gives remainder.

10. // performs integer/floor division.

11. Lists, tuples, strings, sets and dictionaries can be iterated.

12. Dictionary normally gives keys when directly iterated.

13. .values() gives values.

14. .items() gives key-value pairs.

15. enumerate() gives index + value.

16. zip() allows parallel iteration.

17. Loop else executes when the loop completes normally.

18. break prevents loop else from executing.

19. An accumulator stores a result.

20. A counter counts something.

